      "id": 118297,
      "name": "Killswitch",
      "username": "Killswitch",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-09-17T13:32:27.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Whenever a card affects a hero's hand or trash, the card refers to \"a hero.\" Since The Sentinels isn't the first deck to deal with multiple targets (Unity's droids, Expatriette's flak jacket, Visionary's projection), I believe there has been no problem with affecting an entire hero's board as far as taking damage. It's always been referred to as hero targets.</p><p>So yeah, I fully understand what a hero TARGET is. I just wasn't sure if each Sentinel in that deck counts toward \"H,\" since they can each be incapacitated, each have a power, etc.</p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:51:11.369Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
