      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Whenever a card affects a hero&#39;s hand or trash, the card refers to &quot;a hero.&quot; Since The Sentinels isn&#39;t the first deck to deal with multiple targets (Unity&#39;s droids, Expatriette&#39;s flak jacket, Visionary&#39;s projection), I believe there has been no problem with affecting an entire hero&#39;s board as far as taking damage. It&#39;s always been referred to as hero targets.</p><p>So yeah, I fully understand what a hero TARGET is. I just wasn&#39;t sure if each Sentinel in that deck counts toward &quot;H,&quot; since they can each be incapacitated, each have a power, etc.</p>",
