      "raw": "[quote=\"xThe Killswitch\"]\n\nWhenever a card affects a hero&#39;s hand or trash, the card refers to &quot;a hero.&quot; Since The Sentinels isn&#39;t the first deck to deal with multiple targets (Unity&#39;s droids, Expatriette&#39;s flak jacket, Visionary&#39;s projection), I believe there has been no problem with affecting an entire hero&#39;s board as far as taking damage. It&#39;s always been referred to as hero targets.So yeah, I fully understand what a hero TARGET is. I just wasn&#39;t sure if each Sentinel in that deck counts toward &quot;H,&quot; since they can each be incapacitated, each have a power, etc.\n\n[/quote]\n\nThey are only incapacitated when their instruction card is flipped. &nbsp;All of the Sentinels have flip side artwork, but those are not incap sides because there are no incap abilities on them. &nbsp;All four have to be flipped, then their character card flips that has the incap abilities, then the Sentinels are incapped.\n",
